\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 NSMutableAttributedString declares the programmatic interface to objects that manage mutable attributed strings. You can add and remove characters (raw strings) and attributes separately, or together as attributed strings. When working with the Application Kit, you must also clean up changed attributes using the various 
\b fix...
\b0  methods. See the Application Kit's specification for this class cluster for more information on fixing attributes.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSMutableAttributedString adds two primitive methods to those of NSAttributedString. These primitive methods provide the basis for all the other methods in its class. The primitive 
\b replaceCharactersInRange:withString:
\b0  method replaces a range of characters with those from a string, leaving all attribute information outside that range intact. The primitive 
\b setAttributes:range:
\b0  method sets attributes and values for a given range of characters, replacing any previous attributes and values for that range.\

\fs14 \

\fs56 \

